*.local
.DS_Store

# `vue-tsc --build` writes these beside the tsconfigs: a cache of the last
# typecheck, not an input to it. Every `pnpm build` rewrites them, so tracking
# them would put churn in every commit that follows a build and return no
# information for it.
#
# They are read only when `vue-tsc --build` runs *without* `--force`. `pnpm
# typecheck` always passes it, but an editor or a bare `tsc -b` does not, and a
# stale cache committed from someone else's machine would have those skip the
# work the cache exists to make cheaper.
*.tsbuildinfo

# `docs/` holds the internal design specification, which is deliberately not
# published. It stays on disk — the code cites it by section number in roughly
# 190 places — but it never enters the repository.
#
# The whole directory is excluded rather than the single file inside it. That is
# not a style choice: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so `docs/` followed by `!docs/DESIGN.md` silently keeps nothing.
# If a file inside has to be tracked, the rule has to start from `docs/*`.
docs/
